    "description": "Wecom Fiber is a broadband network platform serving residential and business customers in Arizona. Its end users are households, enterprises, and community institutions that require fiber-based internet access and communications services. The model is asset-heavy and contracted, with value supported by network buildout, customer relationships, and local market density. FCC materials tied to the ownership structure show that Searchlight Fiber Alliance and related entities control the investment vehicle around Wecom, and that GIC's Epsom Investment Pte. Ltd. held a 46.74% equity interest in the Searchlight Fiber Alliance structure in 2024. The reviewed materials did not disclose Wecom's revenue or the exact full capitalization of the broader sponsor structure. Searchlight invested in Wecom in 2023 and the ownership structure was subsequently reflected in FCC public notices.",
